			"Message": "style(Output): Normalize esbuild output with imports-first shim ordering and 2-space indent\n\nRe-align all compiled artifacts under Configuration/ and Source/ to a consistent esbuild output format. Three structural changes across all files:\n\n1. Move `__defProp`/`__name` helper shim declarations BELOW all static import statements. The previous helpers-first preamble (applied in e2bbb5e8) placed the shims before imports, which caused a forward-reference hazard in some modules where the dynamic import of `@tauri-apps/api/event` in `TauriMainProcessService` references symbols evaluated at module-load time before the shim variables are declared.\n\n2. Normalize indentation to tab-style (2-space visible width) consistent with the preceding pass's conventions; tabs produce narrower diffs against upstream VS Code source.\n\n3. Standardise expression formatting: collapse multi-line arrow function bodies and object property values where line length permits, add trailing commas consistently to final array/object entries, consolidate empty function bodies, and format export blocks with one binding per line.\n\nNo runtime behaviour changes; the transform pipelines (Replace, Rewrite, Inject, Strip, Patch, Instrument), copy plugins, polyfill shims (Process, FileSystem, IPC, NativeModule, ChildProcess, SharedProcess), service stubs (TauriMainProcessService, CELExposeAccessor, NullTelemetry, NullUpdate, NullExtensionGallery, CELSearchService, CELSharedProcessService), and the Rest compiler plugin are semantically identical before and after.",
			"SHA": "ddf9b2c2db0896e7160c96f946d36c62190bc393"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T05:34:23Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				751,
				4
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Expose IQuickInputService through CEL service accessor\n\nAdd the QuickInput service key to the CEL ExposeAccessor map, resolving IQuickInputService from the VS Code platform service layer via InstantiationService. This enables CEL consumer code (Cocoon extension host, Wind service layer) to invoke quick-pick UI dialogs through the standard service accessor pattern.\n\nNormalize the esbuild output config formatting in Output.js to 2-space indentation with collapsed arrow functions and try/catch blocks, aligning with the project-wide convention applied in recent style passes. No functional change to the build pipeline.\n\nThe Accessor.js sourcemap is updated accordingly.",
			"SHA": "07c4f166c0f974e92e82f20bb34a05530b817fa7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T04:08:25Z",
